Assume now that $j=1,2,\ldots,m-1$.
From expression (\ref{eq5}) we have that
\[
  (a_{0} + p a_{1} + \cdots + p^{j} a_{j}) r_{j} - t_{j}
  =
  p^{j+1} h,
  \quad \text{for some $h \in \mathbb{Z}$},
\]
so, $p \mid (t_{j} - a_{0} r_{j})$.
Therefore, $a_{0} r_{j} \equiv_{p} t_{j}$ and using the fact that $r_{j} \not\equiv_{p} 0$, we obtain that $a_{0} \equiv_{p} r_{j}^{-1} t_{j}$.
