The decisive result is external but directly about this paper’s protocols: Micheli–Weger prove the Section 3 CLR/SAP scheme breakable in polynomial time, and Khathuria–Micheli–Weger give an explicit linear-decomposition attack on the Section 4 DHDP/EGDP schemes by solving an \(m^2\times m^2\) system over \(\mathbb Z/p^m\mathbb Z\). That second attack is \(O(m^6)\) ring operations (equivalently \(O(m^8\log^2 p)\) bit operations) and computes the exchanged secret. This eliminates a Track A claim; I’m recording the Step 0 rejection rather than manufacturing misleading gate reports.
