Rejected at Step 0; no generator was shipped.

G and V are feasible through planted ring elements and exact multiplication. H is not:

- The Section 3 SAP/CLR protocol has a polynomial-time congruence-system attack.
- The Section 4 DHDP/EGDP protocols reduce to an \(m^2\times m^2\) modular linear system, costing \(O(m^6)\) ring operations. [Cryptanalysis paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/1810.02964)
- The original paper provides no distributional hardness theorem for literal private-factor recovery. [Original paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/1606.05457)
- Track B is also unsuitable: the natural compact certificate exceeds the answer cap where the mechanical attack becomes costly, and no paper-backed sub-300-operation shortcut exists.

The complete triage and rationale are recorded in [REJECTED.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1606.05457/REJECTED.md).
